<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Garland returns one week after intake and is seen by Dr. Grünewald of addiction medicine on the same day. She has taken secobarbital 200 mg at bedtime from the seven-day supply on six nights; on one night before a recording session she took a third capsule when she could not sleep, and she told us so herself. She has had no daytime shakes, sweats, or seizure-like episodes. She has taken dextroamphetamine 10 mg each morning and no extra doses, and she has felt flat and tired in the afternoons. She has taken sertraline 25 mg daily without nausea or headache. She brought 38 unused secobarbital capsules and 22 dextroamphetamine tablets from earlier prescriptions, which she placed in the pharmacy take-back box with the nurse today. She keeps this week&apos;s supply in a locked box. She has two weeks free of performances from next week and would like to use them for the change. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Secobarbital</td><td>200 mg at bedtime on six nights; 300 mg on one night</td></tr><tr><td>Withdrawal symptoms</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Dextroamphetamine</td><td>10 mg each morning; no extra doses</td></tr><tr><td>Sertraline</td><td>25 mg daily for a week; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Take-back</td><td>38 secobarbital capsules and 22 dextroamphetamine tablets returned today</td></tr><tr><td>Work</td><td>Two weeks without performances from next week</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

